# reference.in: this family's reference requirements, resolved to the exact, hashed reference.lock
# beside this file by `python -m rcp_ndcg_test.jobs.reference_lock` (owner decision 35). The tool
# constrains torch and the CUDA stack to the engine image's freeze; every other pin installs into
# the family's reference venv and takes precedence over the image's copy. Never edit the lock by hand.
# own-torch: true
# own-torch-evidence: the checkpoint's own requirements.txt at the pinned revision pins torch==2.11.0 and torchvision==0.26.0 beside flash-linear-attention 0.5.1 (a compiled extension); the card's published path is the reference, so the family owns its stack
# The reference environment for recipes/topk-embed-v1/reference.py, in ITS OWN
# python (never the harness's process, never the engine image):
#   pip install -r reference.lock
# The wave runner points --reference-python at this environment (the node's bootstrap
# installs it); the reference subprocess runs while the engine on that slot is up.
# `--mode render` needs only huggingface_hub and tokenizers (it reads the pinned config.json,
# tokenizer_config.json, sentence_bert_config.json and tokenizer.json, and runs the card's cut
# in the tokenizers library) and runs in any interpreter that has them.
#
# These are the checkpoint's own requirements.txt pins at revision
# e54485ebab921f2c18c4d092b3f4c40dcca26781 -- the model card's published path is
# sentence-transformers MultiVectorEncoder over the checkpoint's trusted code.  The family is
# own-torch, so the bootstrap builds its reference venv WITHOUT --system-site-packages
# (jobs/bootstrap.sh) and installs exactly these pins: the image's transformers is never involved.
# E2 round 9 pinned transformers==5.9.0, the checkpoint's own release, after the remote
# hf_backbone.py:111 call `self.chunk_gated_delta_rule(...)` died on the image's stack with
# `AttributeError: 'PackedGatedDeltaNet' object has no attribute 'chunk_gated_delta_rule'`:
# 5.9.0's `Qwen3_5GatedDeltaNet.__init__` assigns that instance attribute
# (`self.chunk_gated_delta_rule = chunk_gated_delta_rule or torch_chunk_gated_delta_rule`,
# modeling_qwen3_5.py:422) and its forward calls it (:535); 5.17.0 removed the attribute (its
# forward calls the module-level `torch_chunk_gated_delta_rule`, :639), whose signature takes
# `**kwargs` and never reads the `cu_seqlens` the remote code passes to keep packed documents
# apart -- delegating the call to the 5.17 name would silently change packed-document numerics.
# The earlier range (>=5.10.4,<5.18.0, "the image's stack") no longer holds: it was written to
# avoid installing transformers into the reference venv, but this family's venv is its own and
# reads nothing from the image.  reference.py's declared `_alias_qwen3_5_layer_type` and
# `_promote_qwen3_5_rope_position_ids` shims are inert under 5.9.0 (it carries `layer_type` and
# the 2-D rope promotion); they stay as the conditional aliases they are.
torch==2.11.0
torchvision==0.26.0
# torch 2.11.0's Linux CUDA stack, pinned here because this family owns its torch (own-torch): torch
# requires `cuda-toolkit[cublas,cudart,cufft,cufile,cupti,curand,cusolver,cusparse,nvjitlink,nvrtc,nvtx]
# ==13.0.2` plus the four nvidia-* wheels below directly.  The bootstrap installs the lock with
# `--no-deps` and the completion installs a planned requirement the same way, so an extras-bearing
# requirement would install only the cuda-toolkit meta-package and leave libcufile.so.0 and the other
# runtime libraries out (the r4 wave's `import torch` failure: `libcufile.so.0: cannot open shared
# object file`).  The versions are torch 2.11.0's own requirements at the pinned revision.
nvidia-cublas==13.1.0.3
nvidia-cuda-cupti==13.0.85
nvidia-cuda-nvrtc==13.0.88
nvidia-cuda-runtime==13.0.96
nvidia-cufft==12.0.0.61
nvidia-cufile==1.15.1.6
